Modifications: the files were modified. The upstream godot-export skill was
rewritten in the house style; GodotPrompter's export-pipeline, mobile and
dedicated-server export material was condensed into SKILL.md and the
references presets-and-cli.md, mobile.md and ci.md (Steam and itch.io parts
left to game-publish; GDScript only, C# dropped). CLI flags, preset options,
environment variables and platform requirements were rechecked against the
Godot 4.7 docs, PRs and the 4.7-stable engine source. Fixed on port:
confidential preset values described as living in export_presets.cfg (they
are in .godot/export_credentials.cfg), PCK encryption described as working
with official templates (it needs custom-built templates), "Linux/X11" preset
names (4.x is "Linux"), web threads attributed to
rendering/threads/thread_model (it is the preset's Thread Support option), the
Shader Baker described as running in --headless CLI exports (it doesn't), the
"headless" feature tag (none exists), GODOT_VERSION "4.3" CI pins (now a
patch-level version matching the project), a version-injection EditorScript
run with --script (EditorScript only runs in the editor), --quit-after
described as milliseconds (it counts frames), and the unverified "Android C#
needs .NET 9" claim (replaced by a pointer to the docs). Cross-references
were renamed to adminhead plugins (game-publish, godot-multiplayer,
godot-csharp, godot-shaders, godot-testing, godot).
